  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Primary path",
      "items": [
        "The handler estimates work, then the admission controller either admits, queues, or returns 429 with Retry-After.",
        "The scheduler atomically reserves estimated work before it proxies an OpenAI-compatible request to one healthy worker.",
        "The streaming proxy forwards bytes while measuring first-token latency, inter-token gaps, usage, and cancellation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Worker ownership & deployment",
      "items": [
        "Workers may be native macOS model servers or Kubernetes-discovered worker pods; both remain upstream of the gateway.",
        "A worker is traffic-eligible only after transport and functional-generation checks; drain state removes it from routing.",
        "Kubernetes discovery is enabled only when WORKER_DISCOVERY=kubernetes; static and external workers remain supported."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Telemetry dependency",
      "items": [
        "The gateway exports OpenTelemetry signals to the collector, which fans traces to Tempo, logs to Loki, and metrics to Prometheus.",
        "Prometheus also scrapes the gateway directly; Grafana is provisioned against the observability services."
      ]
    }
  ]
